'''Icy Road'''{{unofficial}} is a [[Spells|spell]] that freezes the air at long distance.
==Description==
The casting seal contains a [[Sigils Explained#Crystalize|Crystalize]] Sigil surrounded evenly by inverted [[Signs Explained#Columns|Columns]] Signs and an unknown sign. Crystalize is likely to be what is freezing the air while Columns is causing the spell’s effect to extend beyond the ring of the seal.

There is a limit to the spell’s range, as [[Euini]] is required to use [[Frozen Path|a different spell]] to maintain the effect once they reach the end of the spell’s radius.{{Ref|m|22|17}}{{Ref|a|13|}}

[[Agott]] references [[Alaira]]’s spell to freeze the air underneath her steps when casting this one. It is unclear if this is the same spell or simply inspired by Alaira's in the moment.{{Ref|m|22|15}}{{Ref|a|13}}
==Usage==
To escape [[Sasaran]]’s reach in the [[Serpentback Cave]] while taking on the [[Sincerity of the Shield]], Agott quickly draws this spell on the ground of the [[Serpentback Cave|Serpentback Road]]. After freezing over the road and its gaps, Richeh erects a stone ‘scale’ from the Serpentback Road and uses [[Boulder Stretch Rope]] to mold and shape stone into handles and a makeshift corral for the [[Myrphon|myrphons]]. Propelling them forward with Agott’s [[Sylph Shoes]], the three apprentices and myrphons slide down the now slippery expanse of the Serpentback Road, evading the effect of the [[Forbidden Magic]] cast upon the road.{{Ref|m|22|15-17}}{{Ref|a|13}}
==Trivia==
*Only part of the spell’s casting seal is shown in the manga, containing the Columns and unknown signs.{{Ref|m|22|15}}
*The anime provides a clearer look of the seal, now revealing its sigil.{{Ref|a|13}}
